## Why

The member summary gives too much space to currency headings and record counts. Put the declared total beside the member identity and use the summary area for two graphs.

## What changed

- Show pound amounts and move the known total to the upper right of the member header.
- Keep the category breakdown and add weekly employment earnings with exact values shown in bar tooltips. Enlarge the chart and combine the registration-week label with its heading.
- Remove declaration and funding count blocks, currency sections, and the counted history link.

## Scope

The member summary and shared member declaration amounts change. The weekly graph groups declarations by registration week because payment dates are unavailable. The API contract and funder page retain their existing behavior.

## Verification

- Frontend check and production build pass. The initial 34 Playwright tests pass. The three member summary browser tests pass after the disclosure and chart layout updates.
- The live Nigel Farage total is £2,323,720.45. All 112 weekly values match an independent Decimal calculation, including 30 weeks with recorded earnings.
- Desktop and mobile screenshots use the running branch with live API data. Mobile has no horizontal overflow or split category amounts.

![Desktop member summary](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd720bfb-3e19-4ee3-8a0f-2719d775cc19)

![Mobile member summary](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d0efabf-41fc-4a45-a84e-a6592cb37de9)
  than synchronizing the copies. Trace changes through producers, serialization,
  consumers, and persistence together.

## Frontend coding policy

- The frontend is largely in a prototype stage so changes can be made freely without much guidance.
- Every PR that changes the UI must include desktop screenshots in its
  description. Capture the affected views from the running application on
  the PR branch after completing the changes.
- Upload screenshots as GitHub attachments with `gh pr create --attach` or
  `gh pr edit --attach`. Use a GitHub CLI version that supports this flag. Never
  commit PR screenshots to the repository. Verify that the attachments render
  in the PR description before marking the PR ready for review.


